Techpack System Architecture Specification
Version 0.1 — Draft

Overview
    Techpack is a multi-device hub inside a backpack to allow for inventory logging, health metric/enviornmental conditions tracking, and peripheral device powering.

    Ruppert-lite is a shell build around utilizing CLI AI's. The shell will be responsible for serializing and logging data from other devices, with the AI component utilizing the logs to make data recollection better and discourage hallucination. Rupert will be the user's primary means of accessing this data when a gui is not active. Long term smart glass integration will allow Ruppert to listen to audio commands/converstations, potentially logging visually identified objects as well,


This document defines the boot architecture, service layout, runtime model, and security policies for the Techpack ecosystem.

Hardware + Boot Architecture-
  Must wakeup from network events, sensor events, or user events.
  Boot order:
    Firmware → Bootloader → Minimal Arch CoreOS → SystemServices → (Screen detected?) → SystemServicesGUI → Runtime/Apps
      Minimal Arch CoreOS
        Reproducable kernal config for x86/ARM for predictable deivce tree overlay-no heavy desktop enviornment loaded, only required packages
    Safe/Reset Mode:
      Boot device with only  logging and network controls
    
System Architecture
  SystemServices: always on, ultra-lite, not directly user friendly
  SystemServicesGUI: loaded only when screen is detected
    #Each device will be capable of connecting to a screen and displaying general info+controls, however they will operate at a lower power without doing so

  SystemServices (Lite, Network-Safe, Always-On)
    These daemons form the Techpack OS layer.
    All devices run these unless restricted by profile.

      tp-sysinfo (System telemetry aggregator)
        Responsibilities:
          CPU load
          memory usage
          battery/thermal
          uptime
          device capability flags
        Notes: Wraps Linux primitives into a unified API.

      tp-netlink (Network presence + device discovery)
        Responsibilities:
          broadcast device ID
          capability flags
          heartbeat
          mesh presence
        Notes: Foundation for inter-device awareness.

      tp-msgbus (Interdevice communication layer)
        Responsibilities:
          distributed IPC
          publish/subscribe channels
          command routing
          telemetry streaming
        Notes: Backbone of Techpack communication.

      tp-authlite (Lightweight identity + key exchange)
        Responsibilities:
          per-device identity keys
          session tokens
          capability-based permissions
        Notes: Prevents impersonation and cross-device compromise.

      tp-packboard (Sensor ingestion daemon)
        Responsibilities:
          packboard sensor data
          wearable telemetry
          environmental readings
        Notes: Runs on wearable/packboard devices.

      tp-syncd (State + file synchronization)
        Responsibilities:
          delta-based sync
          config propagation
          selective log sharing
        Notes: rsync-lite optimized for Techpack.

      tp-ruppertlog (Distributed logging backend)
        Responsibilities:
          JSONL append
          schema registry
          log streaming
        Notes: Backend for Ruppert-lite.

      tp-configd (Configuration + policy enforcement)
        Responsibilities:
          device profiles
          runtime flags
          mode switching (low-power, lockout, etc.)
        Notes: Central policy engine.

      tp-healthstats (Health + fitness metrics engine)
        Responsibilities:
          hydration
          caloric burn
          sleep flags
          heart rate trends
        Notes: Converts raw sensor data into meaningful metrics.

      tp-updater (OTA updates for Techpack services)
        Responsibilities:
          version tracking
          patch deltas
          service restarts
       Notes: Does NOT update the OS — only Techpack modules.

  SystemServicesGUI (Screen-Detected Only)
    -Device dependent Screens optional
    -Smartglass specific interpreations of programs

      tp-dashboard: Unified UI for telemetry, packboard, health, and network.

      tp-notify: Notification center + toast manager. 

      tp-settings-ui: Graphical configuration editor.

      tp-filebrowser: Lightweight file navigator.

      tp-visualizer: Charts, graphs, packboard maps, health visualizations.

Runtime / Apps Layer
  Ruppert-lite
    Responsibilities:
        logger
        data access point
        query engine
        historical metrics store
        Never an authority, only used for retrival of logs/data or to run commands
    This is the “Techpack brain.”
  Pacman Tools
    Contains:
      Code
      techpack-tools
      techpack-services
      techpack-gui
    Any device can install these to join the ecosystem.

Config + Policy Architecture
  Predefined file access
  Ex
    workstation
    brainboard
    laptop
    packboard
    wearable
    server
    browse (profile including GUI, internetbrowser+adblock, no persistent memory changes)
    guest (for when unregistered devices are added on network)

Local Logs
  Each device maintains:
    system logs (journald)
    Techpack logs (tp-ruppertlog)
    health logs (tp-healthstats)
    Sync rules determine what is shared.

Segregated Permissions Structure
  per-device identity keys
  capability flags
  profile-based restrictions
  sandboxing via systemd + namespaces
  tp-msgbus ACLs

  Example:
    A hacked wearable cannot modify workstation configs or impersonate another device.

